#!/usr/bin/env bash
# RETIRED. `ai-glm-agent` ran GLM inside a Claude Code child process with
# --no-session-persistence, so every call started a brand-new conversation.
# It has been replaced by `ai-glm`, which keeps named GLM sessions alive in a
# local OpenCode server.
#
# This stub fails on purpose. One-shot calls cannot be mapped onto named
# persistent sessions without silently inventing a session name, which would
# hide the very continuity the replacement exists to provide.
cat >&2 <<'MSG'
ai-glm-agent has been replaced by ai-glm.

  ai-glm new <name> --prompt-file FILE     start a named GLM review session
  ai-glm ask <name> --prompt-file FILE     continue that same session
  ai-glm implement <name> --prompt-file F  scoped write run in a throwaway worktree
  ai-glm list                              see existing sessions
  ai-glm doctor                            check the installation

Sessions are per repository and per calling agent, and they persist across
server restarts. See docs/glm-opencode.md.
MSG
exit 1
